WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:14.180
Hello, my name is Lachina Robinson and I'm a sports broadcaster for ESPN.

00:14.180 --> 00:20.700
I am so excited to be joining Melissa Dawn-Simkins and the Velvet Suite as a founding ambassador

00:20.700 --> 00:22.900
for athleadership.

00:22.900 --> 00:27.500
You're probably wondering what a basketball analyst has in common with business leaders.

00:28.200 --> 00:34.100
When I say the word agility, I hope that resonates with you because it definitely resonates with

00:34.100 --> 00:36.740
me and I will tell you how.

00:36.740 --> 00:41.140
As a basketball analyst, it is my job to be the expert on the broadcast.

00:41.140 --> 00:47.020
Leading up to a game, I spend countless hours watching film, interviewing players and coaches,

00:47.020 --> 00:52.620
studying statistics, diving into the rules of the game, learning every aspect of the

00:52.620 --> 00:54.940
entire event.

00:54.940 --> 01:00.980
My specific function as the color on the broadcast is to explain and analyze why things

01:00.980 --> 01:02.580
are happening.

01:02.580 --> 01:05.880
Why does player A have 30 points?

01:05.880 --> 01:08.940
Why is team B in a zone defense?

01:08.940 --> 01:12.200
Why did coach A just call a timeout?

01:12.200 --> 01:15.460
What does it mean when the officials call travel?

01:15.460 --> 01:21.180
I am teaching by taking the viewer behind the veil into the minds of the players, coaches,

01:21.180 --> 01:27.260
officials, even the fans, to explain why certain events are taking place and hopefully

01:27.260 --> 01:30.280
make the game more enjoyable.

01:30.280 --> 01:35.900
The definition of agility is the ability to think and understand quickly.

01:35.900 --> 01:41.140
There are hundreds of thousands and sometimes millions of people watching a sporting event

01:41.140 --> 01:43.900
on television at any given time.

01:43.900 --> 01:49.860
And it's my job to understand what is happening very quickly and to be able to communicate

01:49.860 --> 01:54.060
that to the audience in the moment as it's happening.

01:54.060 --> 01:59.420
Talk about pressure, but you get it because it is essential that you are equipped with

01:59.420 --> 02:01.860
this tool as a business leader.

02:01.860 --> 02:07.460
Let me give you an example of how agility comes into play in my day to day.

02:07.460 --> 02:12.660
In that high pressure situation with millions of viewers watching a game, I have prepared

02:12.660 --> 02:16.260
for what I expect to happen in the game.

02:17.260 --> 02:22.900
Sure, nothing in sports ever happens the way we expect, but that doesn't change my role.

02:22.900 --> 02:25.140
And that is where agility comes in.

02:25.140 --> 02:31.940
As a leader, we can prepare for the moment and do the diligence required to be an expert,

02:31.940 --> 02:37.740
but nothing can prepare you for the moment of having to change course under pressure.

02:37.740 --> 02:43.220
To communicate to an audience, to your staff, to those who follow your command that something

02:43.220 --> 02:51.260
else is happening, something I didn't specifically prepare for, but I couldn't predict it.

02:51.260 --> 03:00.260
However, because I have trained, I know that I can find my way and make the changes necessary.

03:00.260 --> 03:05.860
Agility takes trust that as an expert, you prepared for a change of plans, that the unexpected

03:05.860 --> 03:10.660
outcome or action isn't the end of your skill set or training.

03:11.100 --> 03:19.180
You don't know how your opponent will game plan for you, but you know that whatever that

03:19.180 --> 03:24.500
looks like, you can think and understand quickly in order to adjust.

03:24.500 --> 03:32.100
You can be agile in reaching your goal, even if you get there in a different way than you expected.

03:32.100 --> 03:36.380
Being agile is critical in situations where you need to adjust.

03:36.380 --> 03:40.120
I hope this helps you in your journey as an athlete.

03:40.120 --> 03:43.120
You have everything you need.

03:43.120 --> 03:48.400
You have prepared, practiced, and now it's time to execute.

03:48.400 --> 03:49.120
Stay agile.

